### SmartWallet Auth Endpoints — example requests
### Use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension, or copy into curl/Postman.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### 1. Signup
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "Test1234!",
  "name": "Test User"
}

### 2. Login
# Copy the accessToken and refreshToken from the response for the next steps.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "testpassword123!"
}

### 3. Refresh
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "PASTE_REFRESH_TOKEN_HERE"
}

### 4. Example of a protected route (once other modules use JwtAuthGuard)
# GET {{baseUrl}}/cards
# Authorization: Bearer PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE
